{{!
    @template theme_saec/components/badge_credential_canvas

    Reusable badge-image + name/title overlay ("credential canvas"). Wraps
    whatever real image a badge already has (imageurl — dynamic per badge,
    resolved server-side from Moodle's own badge image storage, never
    hardcoded to one specific credential) with a centered text zone for the
    recipient's full name and the credential's title.

    The overlay's position (see scss/saec/_badges.scss) is calibrated to
    pix/badges/badge_python_template.png's own empty content rectangle —
    measured directly from the real 1000×1000 PNG, not guessed. A badge
    using a different image with no such empty zone still renders
    correctly underneath; the text simply overlays wherever that image's
    own artwork happens to sit in that same relative area.

    Used by:
    - templates/core_badges/issued_badge.mustache (public verification page,
      /badges/badge.php?hash=...).
    - templates/components/badge_detail_body.mustache (the "Mi Mochila de
      Insignias" detail modal, issued-badge branch only).

    Example context (json):
    {
        "imageurl": "https://example.org/pix/badges/badge_python_template.png",
        "recipientname": "Ana García Méndez",
        "credentialtitle": "Microcredencial en Python"
    }
}}
<div class="saec-badge-credential-canvas">
    <img class="saec-badge-credential-canvas__frame" src="{{{ imageurl }}}" alt="">
    <div class="saec-badge-credential-canvas__overlay">
        <span class="saec-badge-credential-canvas__name">{{ recipientname }}</span>
        <span class="saec-badge-credential-canvas__title">{{ credentialtitle }}</span>
    </div>
</div>
